# kasm-catalog.trivyignore — expiring trivy exceptions for THIRD-PARTY
# kasmweb/* catalog images only (build/kasm-catalog.txt). Same policy as
# .trivyignore (SEC-44): every entry needs reason/approver/expires (<= 30
# days), enforced by .github/scripts/check-trivyignore.sh and by trivy's
# native exp: in the generated effective file that scan-kasm-catalog.sh
# passes to the gate. Exceptions are only acceptable for findings whose
# code path is dormant under the TinyCDI runtime contract.

# reason:   openssl DTLS-handshake info disclosure; KasmVNC serves
#           TLS-over-TCP on :8443 only (udp.port pinned 0, NetworkPolicy
#           allows TCP only), so the DTLS path is unreachable. Bump the
#           digest to the next -rolling-weekly carrying openssl
#           >= 3.0.2-0ubuntu1.30 instead of re-approving.
# approver: devin
# expires:  2026-10-30
CVE-2026-84782
